# TwinGrid frontend environment. Copy to .env (dev) or .env.production (build).
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time --
# changing them requires a rebuild, and NOTHING here is secret. Never put a real
# credential in a VITE_ variable.
#
# People sign in with their own account on the sign-in screen (the backend issues
# a short-lived access token and a rotating refresh token). There is no shared
# login baked into the app and no self-registration screen: an administrator
# creates accounts.

# REQUIRED for a production build. Backend base URL, no trailing slash. The
# WebSocket URL is derived from it (https -> wss). `npm run build` fails if this
# is unset or points at localhost (see vite.config.ts); it warns on plain http://.
# In `npm run dev` only, an unset value falls back to http://localhost:8000.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# OPTIONAL but recommended in production. URL that receives runtime error
# reports as a JSON POST (see src/lib/errorReporter.ts). Any HTTP collector or
# log drain works; this repo ships no receiver. Unset = console-only.
VITE_ERROR_REPORT_URL=

# OPTIONAL, DEVELOPMENT ONLY. With BOTH set, `npm run dev` signs in as this
# account automatically so you skip the sign-in screen while developing. They are
# not read by a production build: they are not required, and the production bundle
# contains neither value (asserted by src/test/bundleScan.test.ts). Use a
# throwaway low-privilege viewer account on a local backend; never a real one.
# (Leave commented out unless you want the auto sign-in.)
# VITE_DEMO_USERNAME=
# VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD=
